sequenceDiagram
  title 05 — Dynamic View: Ari's Reservation Attempt
  autonumber
  actor Ari as Ari (S23, ari@example.invalid)
  participant Web as Web Application
  participant Auth as AuthContext
  participant Reserve as ReservationService
  participant DB as Workshop Database
  participant Mail as University Mail

  Ari->>Web: Select published W17, click Reserve
  Web->>Auth: Validate signed-in session
  Auth-->>Web: verified StudentId S23, name, email
  Web->>Reserve: reserve request for W17 and S23
  Reserve->>DB: Begin transaction and find reservation W17/S23
  DB-->>Reserve: none
  Reserve->>DB: Lock W17 and read capacity 3, reserved 2
  DB-->>Reserve: seat available
  Reserve->>DB: Insert reservation W17/S23 and commit
  DB-->>Reserve: success, remaining seats 0
  Reserve->>Mail: Request confirmation to ari@example.invalid
  Mail-->>Reserve: unavailable
  Reserve-->>Web: succeeded, remaining seats 0, email unavailable
  Web-->>Ari: Reservation succeeded, confirmation email unavailable

  Note over DB: Stored before W17 reservations are S21 and S22 and Ari is absent
  Note over DB: Stored after W17 reservations are S21 S22 and S23 and capacity remains 3
  Note over Reserve,Mail: No automatic retry and the committed seat is retained per R6
